-- chem/inertiasound.cub — the sign that the inertia engine (chem/inertia.cub) counts, proved. Jacobi's rule reads
-- the number of negative eigenvalues of N as the number of negative pivots of N = LDLᵀ, the k-th pivot being
-- D_k/D_{k−1}, a quotient of consecutive leading minors, whose sign is the sign of the product D_{k−1}·D_k. The
-- engine counts a sign change at step k when bit-eq (bz-pos D_{k−1}) (bz-pos D_k) is false. Proved here, for
-- nonzero binary integers in canonical form: when that test is true the product is positive, and when it is false
-- the product is negative (its negation positive), so every change counted is a negative pivot and every step not
-- counted a positive one. Not proved here: that the engine's minors are N's leading principal minors (Sylvester's
-- identity, which makes Bareiss's divisions exact) and the assembly of the congruence N = LDLᵀ over lists.
import "inertia.cub"

import "h2ground.cub"

